      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "We met with the Sales Consultant and agreed to the recommended system and paid our deposit of $400 on 3rd August 2016.I called Supercharged Solar in mid October 2016 and we were advised the installation would be in 2-4 weeks. I called them again on 6th December 2016 and I was advised I would not be getting the Risen panels originally promised but they could not advise which panels we would get. On 8th December 2016 we were advised by email from Supercharged Solar that our installation was scheduled for the week commencing 19th December 2016 and that someone would be in contact with us soon.By 11th January 2017 (5 months after signing the contract) we decided not to proceed with this company and requested a refund of our deposit. On 13th January 2017 someone from the Supercharged Solar office called me to arrange an installation date. I didn't want them to carry out the work and we were promised the refund would be made.I sent two further follow up emails during May 2017 about our refund but still have not received any response whatsoever from Supercharged Solar.I have now lodged a Consumer Complaint with the Dept. of Commerce to have my deposit refunded.We were very patient but I would not recommend this company to anyone.",
